From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 14:04:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/26] isolate: unify bounded context reuse

Add one bounded, isolate-local cache for reusable database-UDF, Convex-runtime action, and HTTP-action contexts. Each module declares the execution kinds it permits through the typed experimental_reuseContext policy; the legacy boolean remains compatible for queries and mutations, while omitted properties remain disabled.

Share resident and in-flight cache capacity across the execution kinds while keeping their cache keys, analyzed metadata, and eligibility checks distinct. Preserve scheduler affinity for a matching context, prefer reuse before worker creation, and expose bounded lifecycle, occupancy, affinity, validation, and memory-pressure metrics.

Reinstall request-owned state for every invocation and validate saved initialization reads before reuse. Carry cancellation through the full execution tree, reject terminated or unsafe candidates, and hold newly warmed action contexts outside the cache until the result is delivered so a dropped caller cannot publish an unobserved context. Keep nested dependency work and existing worker-capacity invariants unchanged.

Remove the startup-time HTTP context-reuse switch and consolidate the adoption contract, design reference, configuration guidance, and cross-patch documentation under context_reuse. The feature remains opt-in at the module boundary and can be rolled back by removing the corresponding policy properties and restarting workers.
